    "reply": "I added `tests/test_payments.py` with 11 standard-library `unittest` tests covering `line_total`, `order_total`, and `refund`. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes, and nothing under `shop/` was changed.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- **`line_total`**: price \u00d7 quantity, zero quantity, and float prices.\n- **`order_total`**: empty order, single-line tax, multi-line subtotal before tax, two-decimal rounding, and that `TAX_RATE` is applied.\n- **`refund`**: subtraction, full refund to zero, and zero refund.\n\nI didn't find a bug, so there are no `expectedFailure` tests. Two things you may want to decide on:\n- `refund` does no validation. It accepts a refund larger than the order total or a negative amount, and the module has no documented rule for either. I tested only the normal cases.\n- The multi-line test uses a tolerance of 0.01 because 32.475 can round either way in floating point. If you want an exact value, the expected rounding rule should be pinned down first.\n\nThe `tests/` directory is untracked, so it still needs to be committed. I haven't committed it since you didn't ask me to.",
